message.content:
You are performing the MANDATORY orphan-interface scan of a whole-repository code review, scoped to the edge/embedded C++ side of the repo at /home/ubuntu/个人学习/AI-powered-Network-Diagnostics. STRICTLY READ-ONLY: never modify, delete, deprecate or create any file; do not touch openspec/, .ai-harness/, or any OpenSpec artifact; do not run builds.

An orphan is a reviewed PRODUCTION surface with no real consumer. A caller that exists only in a test/fixture does NOT count as a consumer. Candidate classes to check:
- internal API/class/method declared for cross-file use whose only caller is a test;
- exported symbols / the C API header client/weaknet_client.h with no representative downstream consumer;
- callback/plugin hooks registered but never dispatched, or dispatched but never registered;
- CLI subcommands/flags that nothing invokes (weaknet-cli subcommands, history_query_tool flags, test binaries shipped as production?);
- configuration keys or env vars parsed but never consulted by a live code path (config.yaml keys, weaknet_config.cpp whitelist keys, WEAKNET_* env vars);
- protocol or persistence shape with only one side implemented (D-Bus methods/signals with no client, edge uplink fields the cloud never reads, SQLite tables nothing queries);
- build targets/install/package rules with no downstream consumer (CMake targets, tools/ci.sh packaging steps);
- eBPF programs (12 .bpf.c under server/src and server/src/bpf) compiled but never loaded, loaded but never read, or attached but never producing output — check each against server/src/monitor_ebpf_plugins.cpp, server.cpp, weaknet_config defaults (bluetooth.a2dp_fusion_enabled=false retires a2dp_media by default — classify deliberately);
- build/deploy scripts superseded by another entrypoint (tools/*.sh, scripts/setup_*.sh, init.sh, .docker/);
- known-legacy areas that may be intentional incubation: a2dp_media/audio_quality/bt_audio_fusion (documented legacy optional capability, kept for compatibility), AI-assisted analysis/ (documented deprecated RAG prototype, no importer). For these, verify the documentation claim (search for any real consumer) and classify as "document as intentional incubation with exit condition" only if truly consumer-less AND documented.

Scope you must cover (state your search scope explicitly in the report): server/src/**, server/include/**, client/**, tools/**, scripts/** (non-harness usage), config.yaml, CMakeLists.txt files, cmake/.

For EACH finding you report you must provide, per the review contract:
1. exact path + symbol with file:line;
2. the exact grep/search you ran and the scope, proving absence of a consumer (e.g. "rg 'symbolName' --type cpp across server/ client/ → only hits: definition + test file X");
3. explicit classification: no caller | test-only caller | dead dispatch | parsed-never-read | superseded-entrypoint | unreachable-artifact;
4. verification it is real production code (not generated/vendor/test asset).
Then give: severity (Critical/Important/Minor), the concrete consequence of leaving it, and ONE recommended disposition: remove | replan with a real consumer | document as intentional incubation (with exit condition).

Do NOT pad: if you cannot verify a candidate, drop it. An empty/partial section is fine. Aim for high-confidence findings only; 5-20 verified findings is a good range. Return the findings ordered by severity as your final report, with a short "scope covered / candidates checked and cleared" list at the end (e.g. which eBPF programs you verified are loaded AND consumed, which config keys you verified are read).

